{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The native values give a 10 ms time constant. An independent simulation reaches 0.09516263 V at 1 ms, below the required 0.62–0.65 V range. All three findings describe this same defect, so I’ll retain the failing check as canonical and link both reviewer findings to it. The five saved tracks each meet the 0.20 mm width requirement."}}
