ent Analysis\n\nvout_1ms            =  9.516263e-02\nvout_5ms            =  3.934694e-01\n\n\nTotal analysis time (seconds) = 0.007\n\nTotal elapsed time (seconds) = 0.009 \n\nTotal DRAM available = 128728.297 MB.\nDRAM currently available = 35839.051 MB.\nMaximum ngspice program size =   21.504 MB.\nCurrent ngspice program size =   13.055 MB.\n\nShared ngspice pages =   11.000 MB.\nText (code) pages =    6.156 MB.\nStack = 0 bytes.\nLibrary pages =    2.254 MB.\n\n\n# Declared fixture requirements (RC low-pass review exercise)\n\nThese are artificial review requirements declared for this demonstration\nfixture. They are not ECU electrical requirements, and they are fixed for the\nwhole demonstration (recorded before any review run).\n\n1. Step response: with an ideal 1 V step at /IN and no external load, the\n   voltage at /OUT at t = 1 ms after the step must satisfy\n   0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V.\n   (Intended design: R1 = 10 kohm, C1 = 100 nF, tau = 1 ms,\n   V(1 ms) = 1 - exp(-1) = 0.6321 V.)\n2. Geometry: every copper track segment on the board must be at least\n   0.20 mm wide. This is a declared geometric requirement for the exercise,\n   not an ampacity or manufacturing guarantee.\n\nScope limits: the ideal R/C simulation establishes only the unloaded step\nresponse. Tolerance, temperature, loading, ADC sampling, EMI and hardware\nbehavior are untested by this fixture.\n\ndrc.json {'execution': 'ok', 'outcome': 'pass', 'summary': 'DRC with schematic parity reported zero issues on the saved board'}\nerc.json {'execution': 'ok', 'outcome': 'pass', 'summary': 'ERC ran on 1 sheet instance(s) with zero violations'}\ngeometry.json {'execution': 'ok', 'outcome': 'pass', 'summary': 'all 5 checked track segment(s) meet the declared 0.2 mm minimum width (narrowest 0.25 mm)'}\nnetlist.json {'execution': 'ok', 'outcome': 'info', 'summary': 'native XML netlist exported from a complete 1-instance hierarchy: 3 component(s), 3 net(s), 0 DNP'}\nrc-step.json {'executi